WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:51.150
<b>Genius Brunch</b>

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:51.150
<b>Taking a Bite Out
of Power Spots!</b>

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:08.110
<b>Aizome Kento        Masunaga Kazuna      Kitakado Tomohisa          Osari Hikaru              Nome Tatsuhiro</b>

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:08.110
Taking a bite out of power spots!

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:12.830
This week, the five of us from B-Project...

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:17.870
Will be bringing you all the news on the 
power and gourmet spots here in Hakozaki.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:19.870
Before us lies the ocean.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.120
Behind us are the mountains.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.620
This is an awesome location.

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.350
I think those of us who were chosen

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:30.600
<b>Ocean Team</b>

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:30.600
for the ocean team will be 
getting much better information.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:34.630
<b>Mountain Team</b>

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:33.520
Don't underestimate the mountain team.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:34.630
Yeah, that's right.

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:37.810
Don't you know Tomo and Kazuna were the

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:41.390
<b>Tomo</b>

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:41.390
<b>Masunaga-kun and Kitakado-kun
From Their Bambi Days</b>

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.830
ultimate brunch reporter duo during their Bambi days?

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:44.240
You won't beat us in our old haunt.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:46.560
Well, you won't beat us, either.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.690
Let's go, Tatsu.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:48.280
Yeah.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.410
Yeah!

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.150
<b>*Not Intended to be a Competition!</b>

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:52.870
Cut!

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:57.610
From here on out, we're going 
to split into two groups for filming.

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:59.260
I look forward to working with you.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:00.130
Yes, sir.

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:02.820
Kitakado-san.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:08.160
This contains everything you'll need, 
like bug spray and sunscreen lotion.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.500
Got it.

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:13.330
How could you join 
the mountain team, Tsubasa?

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:14.860
You're so cold.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:17.100
Th-That wasn't my intention.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.510
Kento, don't tease her.

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:23.020
Sorry. I wish I could be 
in two places at once.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:27.380
We're fine. After all, this is our old home.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:28.090
Right?

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:30.420
Yeah.

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:34.880
Um, about our next shooting location...

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:51.530
Hikaru.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:53.570
Oh.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.180
We're leaving already?

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:57.520
You don't look well.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:59.470
Did you take your medicine?

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:03.720
Oh, yeah. I actually forgot it.

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.230
What? We're staying overnight for this shoot.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:10.730
I'll be fine. I promise 
I won't let it affect filming.

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:13.580
Let me know if anything comes up.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.240
I'm counting on you.

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:52.480
<b><i>BULLET of the Heart</i></b>

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:55.040
Anyway, that's the plan.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:55.750
Got it.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:02.130
Safe.

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:05.010
Th-Thank you.

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:07.140
Let's start shooting.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:08.100
Okay.

00:04:12.070 --> 00:04:13.440
Safe.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.560
Not safe. Don't get too excited.

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:18.570
Okay.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.200
It's cold.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.700
As long as we're here, 
we should purify our entire bodies.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.950
You guys are too much.

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:30.280
There.

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:32.080
Cut!

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:35.510
Did the equipment get wet?

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:37.710
It's not a problem.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.680
You've got a lot on you.

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:43.620
It's fine. You can use it.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:51.230
Hmmm...

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:53.230
Ta-da!

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:56.000
They've got shiitake ice cream. 
Isn't that amazing?

00:04:53.230 --> 00:05:01.230
<b>Hakozaki Mountain
Panorama Rest House</b>

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:58.440
You're going to eat that?

00:04:58.440 --> 00:04:59.610
Of course.

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:01.810
It's delicious!

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:02.490
Here.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:05.200
No, thanks. I'm good.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.670
Tsubasa-chan, what's that?

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:10.160
Wasabi ice cream.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.790
Give me a bite.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:13.040
What?

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:16.870
It's so good. They're both so tasty.

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:20.410
Couldn't we include this 
in our gourmet report?

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:22.340
<b>Hakozaki Mountain
Panorama Rest House</b>

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:22.340
People would love it.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:23.810
Excuse me!

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:28.220
These whitebait croquettes are freshly fried.

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:36.080
They're good. This is my first time 
eating croquettes by hand.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:38.230
You really are different from us common folk.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:39.620
Want some?

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:42.300
You can't have any.

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:50.730
My croquette!

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:53.160
Cut!

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:56.750
Nice, Masunaga-kun. That was great.

00:05:58.010 --> 00:05:59.660
Thank you.

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:01.170
Here. Have another.

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:01.970
What?

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:04.680
It's okay. Nobody's eaten this one yet.

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:06.300
I just bought it.

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:08.830
Thanks.

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:10.680
You guys can have some, too.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.180
These are from Kitakado-san.

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:20.650
You can have mine.

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:24.770
I see.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:29.070
These are the Buddha's Footsteps.

00:06:29.710 --> 00:06:31.570
These are footsteps?

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:32.410
Question!

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:37.070
Is there any legend associated with these, 
like touching them cures all illnesses?

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:38.530
No.

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:39.710
There isn't?

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:43.840
Godaiso is much better 
for you if you're sick.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.090
Godaiso?

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:49.150
It's been consumed in this region for ages.

00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:52.470
It's said to cure all illnesses.

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:55.420
Because it grows on steep cliffs,

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:58.460
it's said that some people 
have lost their lives trying to get it.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:02.230
Really? Sounds like some
kind of legendary herb.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:10.500
Do you think that story was true?

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:12.760
It's probably like a fairy tale.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:16.170
There's no such thing as 
an herb that can cure any illness.

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:18.970
Yeah, you're right.

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:24.970
Apparently, your wishes will 
come true if you write them on shells

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:27.010
and make an offering of them at this lighthouse.

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:30.050
Shouldn't we write something, then?

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.280
What did you write?

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:33.730
What? Oh...

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:36.140
That I hope we fall in love with each other.

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:38.600
Really? Then I...

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:41.820
will wish for your wish to come true.

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:44.270
Th-Thank you.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.860
<b>May Your Wish Come True!</b>

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:47.860
Okay, cut!

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:51.250
You'd just break up with her right away.

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:55.060
You're always so nice, Kazu.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:56.970
I'm not that nice.

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:00.120
What?

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:05.640
Nothing. I was just thinking 
that you really like Tomo.

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:08.130
What? Wh-Where did that come from?

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:10.330
You thought we didn't know?

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:14.320
You've been awkward around 
each other for a while, especially you.

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:18.480
Tsubasa was worried about it, too, 
so I've been watching you.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:20.480
But I see now.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:24.140
If you've been watching us, 
then you'd know that's not the case.

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:26.550
You know better than
anyone else what's going on.

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:28.570
I'll report my findings to Tsubasa.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:30.140
She'll probably be relieved.

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:31.650
I said it's not like that!

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:35.290
It's okay, Kazu. I understand.

00:08:36.260 --> 00:08:37.260
Understand what?

00:08:38.390 --> 00:08:39.800
Give me a break.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:43.820
He's not usually so distraught.

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:46.810
Kento, don't tease him so much.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:49.750
It must be hard for you, too.

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:55.090
Not really.

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:58.570
We look forward to staying with you.

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:00.510
Thank you.

00:09:00.810 --> 00:09:02.750
This is your room.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:04.790
It's bigger than I heard.

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:06.520
Tsubasa, you're not staying with us?

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:08.580
O-Of course not.

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:11.680
Then maybe I'll go hang out in your room.

00:09:11.680 --> 00:09:12.290
Good idea.

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:14.280
Y-You can't do that.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:16.490
How did the mountain shoot go?

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:18.180
Pretty smoothly.

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:21.230
Although Hikaru got caught in a spiderweb 
and made a huge fuss about it...

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:25.770
Not just spiderwebs! 
I got spiders on my face, too!

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:27.290
Yikes...

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.110
How did the ocean shoot go?

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:32.320
I think our gourmet content 
was better than the power spots.

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:34.730
There were lots of interesting foods,

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:37.300
but I was surprised by the shrimp 
soft serve they brought out at the end.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:39.700
Shrimp soft serve? I want some of that!

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:42.310
Hikaru-kun, you're always eating ice cream.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:45.360
The local ice cream flavors 
are the true joy of any trip.

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:47.680
Let's ask if we can stop by 
on our way home tomorr—

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:53.230
Hikaru-kun?

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:54.230
Hikaru.

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:56.400
Hikaru, are you okay?

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:58.860
Hikaru-kun?

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:04.880
Sorry for making you worry.

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:07.250
I guess I'm tired from running around.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:09.530
Who coughs up blood from running around?

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:12.130
We should get you out of filming tomorrow.

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:13.860
Don't—

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:18.590
We'll decide what to do about you later.

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:20.700
For now, you should see a doctor.

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:22.490
I'll ask where the hospital is.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:23.640
Wait.

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:28.140
Hikaru, are you hiding something from us?

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:32.940
It's been bothering me since then.

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:36.190
Osari-kun, how are you feeling?

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:38.450
Huh? Oh, yeah.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:39.950
I'm fine.

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:45.240
It's nothing.

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:46.570
Hikaru-kun.

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:48.270
Tatsu.

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:54.850
Hikaru, we should tell them.

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:57.760
There's nothing to say.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:01.380
If you keep quiet now, you'll just 
cause more of an uproar later.

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:04.360
Then you really won't 
be able to keep working.

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:12.880
Kitakado's right.

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:17.900
Hikaru has been sick
since before he debuted.

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:20.200
It can't be cured by modern medicine.

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:21.950
It's incurable.

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:27.410
If he puts too much strain on his body, 
his symptoms advance rapidly.

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:29.410
No...

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:33.610
But I can live a normal life 
as long as I take my medicine.

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:35.840
I can be an idol.

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:37.580
You can be an idol? Hikaru...

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:40.810
You guys haven't noticed until now, right?

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:42.180
Well...

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:44.810
I just forgot my medicine today.

00:11:44.810 --> 00:11:48.980
It's no big deal. I'll feel better 
after a good night's sleep.

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:51.020
You're going to keep filming tomorrow?

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:52.190
You must be joking.

00:11:52.190 --> 00:11:54.610
I don't want to miss any work.

00:11:54.610 --> 00:11:55.560
Hikaru.

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:59.160
Please, Leader. I'm begging you.

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:00.950
I'd like to ask that you let him go, as well.

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:03.200
Don't tell anyone about this.

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:09.700
Huh? Where are Osari-kun and Sumisora-san?

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:12.250
Hikaru has a stomachache.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:14.710
Sumisora-san is staying with him.

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:18.710
Too bad. Osari-kun was excited 
about the food report.

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:20.890
Will he be okay tomorrow?

00:12:20.890 --> 00:12:22.840
Yes, it won't be a problem.

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:25.170
Sorry for making you worry.

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:30.850
Hikaru must be frustrated that 
he won't get to eat this delicious fish.

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:32.850
Speaking of fish...

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:34.600
Yeah, it brings back memories.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:36.090
Why?

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:41.870
During one of our brunch report shoots, 
we tried catching fish with our bare hands.

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:43.860
But instead of catching fish...

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:49.080
We were thrown into a fish 
tank and nibbled at instead.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.480
Right, Shibata-san?

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:52.960
Sorry, sorry.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:55.340
What? Shibata-san, you filmed that?

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:58.110
How could you do that to such handsome men?

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:01.230
Shibata-san toughened us up in other ways, too.

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:02.040
Right?

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:02.840
Yeah.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:06.070
Shibata-san, do you still have those costumes?

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:06.070
<i>They're a good duo.</i>

00:13:06.070 --> 00:13:08.340
Yeah, they're at the office.

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:09.750
<i>They're making them forget all about Hikaru.</i>

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:09.910
They're my treasure.

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:13.190
Seriously? I want to see those.

00:13:13.190 --> 00:13:15.320
I doubt we'd fit in them, anymore.

00:13:13.470 --> 00:13:14.320
Nome?

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:17.810
Sorry. I'm going to go switch with Sumisora.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:17.810
Yeah.

00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:20.630
My stomach hurts.

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:24.240
I told you to take your medicine.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:26.180
It tastes bad. I don't like it.

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:28.280
Get me some godaiso.

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:30.550
You're being stubborn again.

00:13:30.550 --> 00:13:32.370
Do you have some godaiso?

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:33.040
What?

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:38.010
No, though apparently, 
we had some generations ago.

00:13:38.490 --> 00:13:39.720
But now...

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:42.060
But it does exist, right?

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:49.430
I slept well.

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:52.870
That's good. You're looking a lot better.

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:56.550
I'm back.

00:13:56.550 --> 00:13:57.640
Welcome back.

00:13:57.910 --> 00:13:59.880
How are you feeling, Hikaru?

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:01.940
I'm all better.

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:04.280
You should rest.

00:14:05.310 --> 00:14:06.610
Here.

00:14:07.060 --> 00:14:08.110
You must be hungry.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:09.380
Rice balls!

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:11.730
Thank you very much.

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:13.870
You should let Nome take care of him.

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:16.370
Tsubasa, you haven't come to see us yet, so...

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:19.080
Huh? Where's Nome?

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:20.030
What?

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:23.800
<i>The legendary herb.</i>

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:26.210
<i>If it really does exist...</i>

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:29.740
<i>I think they said it grows on steep cliffs.</i>

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:39.980
<i>If that... If that's the godaiso...</i>

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:43.480
<i>If that's the godaiso, then... Hikaru!</i>

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:51.990
Tatsuhiro isn't anywhere at the inn.

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:53.990
He's not answering his phone, either.

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:56.250
It's been four hours since he left.

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:58.000
He's totally missing.

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:00.000
Tatsu...

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:02.060
Let's go outside to look for him.

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:04.840
Hikaru, you stay here.

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:05.810
But—

00:15:05.810 --> 00:15:07.840
Let us handle Nome-san.

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:09.780
Tsubasa, you're staying here, too.

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:10.510
What?

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:14.500
We can't let a girl go out at this hour.

00:15:14.500 --> 00:15:19.120
We need you to take care of 
Hikaru and handle the staff.

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:23.370
We can't let them think 
B-Pro is riddled with problems.

00:15:24.030 --> 00:15:25.270
I understand.

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:26.530
Good girl.

00:15:32.750 --> 00:15:34.880
I'm going with them.

00:15:34.880 --> 00:15:36.120
Hikaru-kun.

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:41.010
I can't help it, but it's weird 
for him to cause this much concern!

00:15:41.010 --> 00:15:43.060
Something must've happened to him!

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:46.130
I understand how you feel, 
but you need to rest.

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:49.090
Just sitting here is far more stressful!

00:15:49.830 --> 00:15:51.060
Hikaru-kun...

00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:56.140
Good work today.

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:57.600
You, too.

00:15:57.600 --> 00:15:59.870
Huh? It's kind of quiet in here.

00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:03.260
Oh, Kitakado-san and 
the others went out for a walk.

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:06.150
Oh, right. The stars are beautiful out here.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.110
Is something wrong?

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:11.390
No. We were just wondering 
how Osari-kun is feeling.

00:16:11.390 --> 00:16:13.450
His stomach seems to have mostly settled.

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:16.280
Um, he's asleep right now, so...

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:19.900
Well, let us know if anything comes up.

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:21.270
Thank you.

00:16:29.650 --> 00:16:30.880
Ow...

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:38.760
Okay. I'm not hurt.

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:43.270
Uh, oh. Did I drop my phone?

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:54.300
Oh, well. It's probably best 
if I wait until it's light out to move.

00:16:56.540 --> 00:17:00.150
I'll definitely bring this home to you, Hikaru.

00:17:02.470 --> 00:17:04.710
Where are you, Tatsu?

00:17:06.180 --> 00:17:09.400
Am I out of place here?

00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:10.630
Good morning!

00:17:12.180 --> 00:17:13.590
Is today your first day?

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:14.880
Y-Yeah.

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:17.090
Seriously? I'm starting today, too.

00:17:17.380 --> 00:17:18.470
Nice to meet you.

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:34.280
<i>I still think back on the 
time we first sang together</i>

00:17:30.470 --> 00:17:31.420
I did it.

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:33.190
You're amazing.

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:43.550
<i>That day my heart pounded so hard 
like my destiny was changing</i>

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:37.340
You scared me!

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:39.530
No, seriously.

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:46.540
Thanks. That makes me really happy.

00:17:49.010 --> 00:18:02.180
<i>Holding dear what we've 
built and built up until now</i>

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:08.560
<i>Our present, our youth, our unwavering bond</i>

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:14.570
<i>To feel it with all our hearts and bodies</i>

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:16.570
Tatsu!

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:18.590
<i>Sing with me</i>

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:19.510
Hikaru?

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:20.870
<i>Shalala, shalala</i>

00:18:20.050 --> 00:18:21.650
What are you doing here?

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:22.180
<i>Let's sing</i>

00:18:21.650 --> 00:18:23.360
Don't be ridiculous!

00:18:22.180 --> 00:18:28.580
<i>Take my hand and let's sing 
a reverberating harmony</i>

00:18:23.390 --> 00:18:27.620
You suddenly disappeared! Do you have 
any idea how worried we've been?

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:29.530
Sorry.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:30.870
<i>Shalala, shalala</i>

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:41.580
<i>If we combine our voices and 
sing together, we will be happy</i>

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:33.960
What are you doing here?

00:18:36.060 --> 00:18:37.350
I came for this.

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:39.940
What? What is that?

00:18:41.170 --> 00:18:43.350
The legendary herb.

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:47.230
It wasn't a fairy tale.

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:50.620
We'll use this to cure you.

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:00.170
You idiot!

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:07.910
Does that solve things?

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:11.950
Jeez... I'm glad nothing happened.

00:19:19.350 --> 00:19:20.480
What is that?

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:23.180
I called them.

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:27.040
Kitakado, you're amazing.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:33.810
What? The legendary herb?

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:35.450
Yeah. Look.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:43.700
Huh? Isn't this mugwort?

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:45.450
<b>Asterids, Asterales, Asteraceae, Asteroideae, Artemisia 
Mugwort</b>

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:46.440
What?

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:47.700
What?!

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:55.340
Apparently, godaiso is just 
a local name for mugwort.

00:19:58.270 --> 00:20:01.230
Tatsuhiro, Hikaru...

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:07.020
I'm sorry, Hikaru. 
I got your hopes up for nothing.

00:20:07.910 --> 00:20:12.580
And that's not all. I worried you 
and stressed you out for nothing.

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:17.110
I just wanted to...

00:20:23.930 --> 00:20:25.450
I'll eat it.

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:29.080
As far as I'm concerned, 
this herb cures all illnesses.

00:20:30.110 --> 00:20:31.170
Hikaru-kun...

00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:35.150
Even if I can't acquire a legendary herb,

00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:39.400
I still have friends who are 
willing to go this far for me.

00:20:40.070 --> 00:20:44.660
That gives me infinite strength 
to fight this illness.

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:49.100
Hikaru...

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:56.980
Hikarun!

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:01.110
Are you okay?

00:21:02.140 --> 00:21:04.070
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:05.590
That's good.

00:21:06.210 --> 00:21:08.630
Guys, what are you doing here?

00:21:09.380 --> 00:21:10.540
Here.

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:13.540
My medicine!

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:16.290
Tomo contacted us last night.

00:21:16.510 --> 00:21:20.620
He asked us to look for the medicine 
Hikaru forgot and bring it to you immediately.

00:21:21.440 --> 00:21:22.920
We were so surprised.

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:27.930
Kore-san suddenly barged into 
our rooms and started searching them.

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:30.690
Once we heard the news, we all helped look.

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:38.190
Sheesh! Why'd you have to ask 
us to come at this hour?

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:40.440
Guys...

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:49.430
Thanks!

00:23:22.710 --> 00:23:25.940
Here we are. Our next stop is this lake.

00:23:25.940 --> 00:23:28.230
What kind of power does this spot grant?

00:23:28.660 --> 00:23:33.050
According to our information, 
legend says it grants a long life.

00:23:33.710 --> 00:23:35.420
Did you take your medicine?

00:23:35.420 --> 00:23:38.070
Yeah, of course. And...

00:23:38.820 --> 00:23:39.810
This mugwort mochi.

00:23:44.730 --> 00:23:45.990
Let's go, Tatsu.

00:23:45.990 --> 00:23:46.860
Okay.

00:23:48.570 --> 00:23:49.990
Th-That's...

00:23:50.630 --> 00:23:52.570
Yeah!

00:23:56.020 --> 00:23:57.280
Can I rest my head on your arms?

00:23:57.280 --> 00:23:59.340
Uh, oh. I'm so awake now, I can't sleep.
